Annotations: |
  A second, independently-verified self-contained Gradle feature module, following the same
  Repository+Dependencies convention as the registration cell: no reference to
  AppDependencies, SignalDatabase, or jobmanager anywhere in its top-level files. The host
  app supplies module dependencies (a PreUploadRepository, an ExoPlayerPool, a
  BlobProvider, and others) through `MediaSendDependencies.Provider` at startup.

---

"MediaSendDependencies()":
  location: MediaSendDependencies.kt
  annotations: |
    Module-local dependency injection point, following the same pattern as
    RegistrationDependencies and the app-wide AppDependencies: this module reaches the host
    app only through the Provider interface supplied at init.
  methods:
    "init(application: Application, provider: Provider)": |
      Installs the application instance and Provider this object exposes through its
      properties. Idempotent — a second call is a no-op if already initialized.
  properties:
    "mediaSendRepository -> MediaSendRepository": |
      The module's data-access layer for media validation, transcoding limits, and sending.
    "preUploadRepository -> PreUploadRepository": |
      Repository for uploading selected media ahead of a send being confirmed.
    "exoPlayerPool -> ExoPlayerPool<ExoPlayer>": |
      Shared pool of video player instances for previewing selected media.
    "blobs -> BlobProvider": |
      Access to the host app's content-provider-backed blob storage.

"MediaSendDependencies.Provider()":
  location: MediaSendDependencies.kt
  annotations: |
    The extension point the host app implements to supply this module's dependencies; passed to
    MediaSendDependencies.init.
  methods:
    "provideMediaSendRepository() -> repository:MediaSendRepository": |
      Supplies the module's `MediaSendRepository` implementation.
    "provideExoPlayerPool() -> pool:ExoPlayerPool<ExoPlayer>": |
      Supplies the shared video player pool.
    "provideBlobs() -> blobs:BlobProvider": |
      Supplies access to blob storage.

"MediaSendRepository()":
  location: MediaSendRepository.kt
  annotations: |
    The module's data-access and business-rule layer for the media-editing/sending flow:
    enumerating device media, validating/filtering selections against size and count limits,
    transcoding-tier lookups, and performing the actual send.
  methods:
    "getFolders() -> folders:List<MediaFolder>": |
      The device's media folders available for browsing.
    "getMedia(bucketId: String) -> media:List<Media>": |
      Media items within a given device folder.
    "validateAndFilterMedia(media: List<Media>, mediaConstraints: MediaConstraints, isStory: Boolean, isMms: Boolean) -> result:MediaValidatorResult": |
      Filters `media` down to what is actually sendable under the given constraints, reporting
      what (if anything) was rejected and why.

      `mediaConstraints`: size/count/type limits to validate against.
    "send(request: SendRequest) -> result:SendResult": |
      Performs the actual send of the finalized media/message selection.
    "getVideoTranscodingTiers(quality: SentMediaQuality) -> tiers:List<TranscodingConfig.QualityTier>": |
      The transcoding quality tiers applicable at the given target `SentMediaQuality`, used to
      estimate upload size before sending.
    "isVideoTranscodeAvailable() -> available:Boolean": |
      Whether video transcoding is currently possible on this device/build.
    "getStorySendRequirements(media: List<Media>) -> requirements:Map<Uri, StorySendRequirements>": |
      Per-item requirements (e.g. minimum resolution) a story send imposes on `media`.
    "checkUntrustedIdentities(recipients: List<MediaSendRecipient>) -> untrusted:List<MediaSendRecipient>": |
      Which of recipients currently have an untrusted (changed, unverified) identity key,
      requiring the user to confirm before sending.
    "getMediaConstraints(quality: SentMediaQuality) -> constraints:MediaConstraints": |
      The active size/count/type constraints for the given (or current, if none is given) target
      quality.

"MediaSendFlowState(recipientId: MediaRecipientId, selectedMedia: List<Media>, sentMediaQuality: SentMediaQuality, editorStateMap: Map<Uri, EditorState>, isSending: Boolean, isSent: Boolean)":
  location: MediaSendFlowState.kt
  annotations: |
    The complete state of the media-editing/sending flow. Fully parcelable for SavedStateHandle
    persistence with no separate serialization step — several fields are intentionally marked
    transient-on-parcel and re-derived from `MediaSendRepository` on restore rather than saved,
    because the repository is their source of truth.

    `recipientId`: destination for single-recipient flows.
    `selectedMedia`: the user's current media selection.
    `sentMediaQuality`: target compression/quality tier for the send.
    `editorStateMap`: per-item editor state (crop, trim, drawing), keyed by media URI.
    `isSending`, `isSent`: guard against a duplicate send being triggered.
  properties:
    "isViewOnceAvailable -> Boolean": |
      Whether the current selection is eligible for view-once (exactly one non-document
      attachment, not a story).
    "isViewOnceEnabled -> Boolean": |
      Whether the current selection will actually be sent as view-once.

"MediaSendFlowViewModel(repository: MediaSendRepository)":
  location: MediaSendFlowViewModel.kt
  annotations: |
    Owns a `MediaSendFlowState` and exposes the operations its screens invoke as the user edits
    and sends a media selection, delegating validation, transcoding, and the actual send to
    `MediaSendRepository`.

    `repository`: the module's data-access layer, injected.
  methods:
    "addMedia(media: Set<Media>)": |
      Adds items to the current selection, subject to `MediaSendRepository`'s validation.
    "removeMedia(media: Media)": |
      Removes a single item from the current selection.
    "setSentMediaQuality(sentMediaQuality: SentMediaQuality)": |
      Changes the target quality tier, re-deriving transcoding-size estimates.
    "toggleViewOnce()": |
      Cycles the view-once toggle, when MediaSendFlowState.isViewOnceAvailable allows it.
    "setMessage(text: String)": |
      Sets the optional caption/message text accompanying the media.
    "performSend()": |
      Validates the current state is sendable and triggers send.
    "send() -> result:SendResult": |
      Performs the send via MediaSendRepository.send and updates flow state to reflect the
      outcome.
    "hasSelectedMedia() -> hasMedia:Boolean": |
      Whether at least one item is currently selected.

---

Author: Goga
CreatedAt: 26/08/26
Description: |
  Documents the media-send feature module's Repository+Dependencies+ViewModel convention,
  including its Provider-based dependency-injection extension point. A leaf cell: verified
